  ; on whatever langWriter is declared to hold.
  ; Do we POSITIVELY know the callee takes `&self`? Only the VARIANT set
  ; answers: it is what the signature was written from. A method missing from
  ; it — an extension, an inherited copy — is unknown, and unknown means the
  ; mutable borrow, which always type-checks.
